/// Behavioral API documentation for the Roadie Roster backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source; reads no state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Roadie Roster Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nBackend for **Roadie Roster**, the new-hire tracking app for Bubba's 33 store #975 in Lake Charles, LA (opening Mon Feb 8, 2027). It stores store configuration, positions (stations) with build-to targets, the opening schedule, checklists, retention settings, roadie cards, kiosk sign-up submissions, access grants, and the phase-2/3 records (orientation check-off, attendance, training groups, trainer notes, leader talks, final sign-offs, alerts).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes application data requires a **signed (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nSigning in is not enough: a principal must be **registered** before any role-guarded call succeeds. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `requestAccess()` once. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n- `requestAccess()` records the caller in the pending list and returns `true` when the caller is already registered (or already pending). It is safe to call repeatedly.\n- An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap on every guarded endpoint: `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- A Kiosk login receives `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up` on every read.\n- An expired access grant (past its access end date) is treated as unregistered.\n\n### First-admin bootstrap\n\nThe app's access model is separate from the platform's shared authorization mixin. The **first principal to sign in** is made an admin by that mixin, but that grant does not by itself create an app Admin. To bridge it, the first caller must call `bootstrapAdmin()` once after signing in:\n\n- `bootstrapAdmin()` grants the caller an app Admin grant **only** when the platform mixin already considers the caller an admin **and** no app Admin grant exists yet. It returns `true` when the caller holds an app Admin grant after the call, `false` otherwise.\n- It is idempotent and safe to call repeatedly; it never grants Admin to a caller the platform does not already consider an admin, and it never creates a second bootstrap Admin.\n- `getMyAccess()` reports only a grant that has actually been persisted in the app's access model. An unregistered caller always receives `null`, so the frontend keeps showing the \"Waiting for approval\" screen; the first platform admin's grant becomes visible here only after `bootstrapAdmin()` persists it.\n- After bootstrap, the first Admin approves everyone else with `approveUser`, selecting a role (no role pre-selected; confirm before granting Manager or Admin). At least 2 admins must exist and the last admin cannot be removed.\n\n## Roles and authorization\n\nRoles: Admin, Store Manager, Training Manager, Leadership, Visiting Manager, Trainer, Kiosk, Integration.\n\n- **Contact set** (phone, email, emergency contact, availability, signatures, date of birth) is returned **only** to Admin and Store Manager. Every other role receives roadie cards with `contactSet = null`, and change-log entries that touch the contact set are filtered out.\n- **Admin**: full access, including store configuration, positions, schedule, checklists, retention, templates, and access management.\n- **Store Manager**: everything except access management; may read the contact set and run the Full export.\n- **Training Manager / Leadership / Visiting Manager**: read-only over non-contact data.\n- **Trainer**: sees only roadies in their approved stations.\n- **Kiosk**: may only call `submitSignup`; every read is rejected.\n- **Integration**: read-only, limited to the Shareable export fields.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Timestamps** are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (matching `Time.now()`).\n- **DateOnly** values are UTC-midnight nanosecond timestamps.\n- **TimeOfDay** values are minutes since midnight, store-local.\n- **TimeZone** is an IANA name; the store uses `America/Chicago`.\n- **PhotoRef** and **SignatureRef** are uploaded object-storage references (text).\n- Optional values are Candid `opt`; absent means `null`.\n- `RoadieStatus` is a variant: `#hired`, `#paperworkDone`, `#oriented`, `#inTraining`, `#certified`, `#needsMoreTime`, `#active`, `#archived`. Phase 1 uses only `#hired`, `#paperworkDone`, `#archived`.\n- `ArchiveReason` is a variant: `#noShow`, `#quitDuringTraining`, `#tookAnotherJob`, `#letGo`, `#other(text)`.\n\n## On-hand counts\n\nOn-hand is **never editable by hand**. It changes only through: approve (+1), archive (-1), rehire (+1), and change position (moves 1). `getDashboard` derives it from non-archived roadies.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A kiosk submission starts `#pending`. A Store Manager reviews it, sets the position/crew/orientation/start date, and signs; only then is the roadie card created and on-hand raised by 1. The submission becomes `#approved(roadieId)` or `#rejected`.\n- `listPendingSignups` returns only `#pending` submissions; poll it to drive the \"Approve new hires\" count.\n- Visiting access ends automatically at its access end date (11:59 PM store time, Central); expired grants are treated as unregistered.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `adjustBuildTo` records each tap as a separate +1/-1 delta, so two managers do not overwrite each other. Retrying a tap applies the delta again — do not auto-retry.\n- `approveSignup` traps when the submission is not `#pending`, so a retry after success is rejected rather than creating a duplicate card.\n- `archiveRoadie` traps when the roadie is already archived; `rehireRoadie` traps when the roadie is not archived.\n- `deletePosition` traps when active roadies reference the position; `deleteScheduleEvent` traps when records reference the event.\n- Every mutation writes a change-log entry (who, what, when).\n\n## Errors\n\nFailures are traps with a human-readable message (for example `Access denied: Admin role required`, `Cannot delete a position with active roadies`, `Cannot assign a minor to a position with a higher minimum age`). A trap rolls back the message's uncommitted state changes.\n\n## Exports\n\n- `buildShareableExport` omits the contact set and is available to Integration and above.\n- `buildFullExport` includes the contact set, is Admin/Store Manager only, and is logged.\n\n## Seeding and roster\n\n- `ensureSeeded()` is an idempotent update call. It re-applies the seeded store data (18 positions totalling 218 build-to, the 12-event opening schedule, store info, checklists and retention settings) only when the store has no positions yet, and returns `true` when it seeded and `false` when the store already had positions. It never overwrites existing data. Any read-capable caller may call it; a Kiosk login cannot.\n- `getRosterSummary()` returns one row per position with `onHand` (non-archived roadies assigned to the position) and `openSpots` (build-to minus on-hand, clamped at zero).\n- `getContactSet(id)` returns an array: Admin and Store Manager receive the roadie's contact set as a one-element array, and every other read-capable role receives an empty array. It never traps for a non-manager and never returns undefined.\n";
  };
};
